<title>USA: Ameritech in marketing pact with UNO-VEN.</title>
<headline>Ameritech in marketing pact with UNO-VEN.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ameritech Corp and UNO-VEN Co reached an agreement allowing the oil company to market the Baby Bell's pre-paid phone cards, UNO-VEN said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The cards will be available at Union 76 gasoline stations in the U.S. Midwest in denominations of $10, $20 and $40, said UNO-VEN. The program is scheduled to begin in January.</p>
<p>Ameritech operates local telephone networks in five Midwestern states. UNO-VEN is a partnership between the affiliates Unocal Corp's Union Oil Co of California and Petroleos de Venezuela S.A.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
